The calibration fit (see \code{\link{calibfit}}) models the relationship
\code{sample_value = intercept + slope * source_value}, whatever the calibration
method used (for the method \code{"desk_inverse"}, the inversion of the
regression is already performed by \code{\link{calibfit}}). The mean isoscape is thus
simply calibrated by computing, in each raster
